LAST_SUCCESS=Task 97 bug#1 root cause CONFIRMED (source + device A/B, --probe-call-stall). SHARED-output stall = up-message-queue overflow → setSuspended → mixer-skips-stream → read counter r freezes → write returns 0 → silence. Trigger chain: client underflow (≥~240ms) → SHARED mixer sends UNTHROTTLED XRUN service event (what=3) every burst into the 128-deep up-msg FIFO → if client doesn't DRAIN it (drain_up_messages, called at top of write_pcm_f32) the FIFO hits 128/128 → "writeUpMessageQueue(): Queue full. Did client stop? Suspending stream. what=3, Shared" → suspended stream skipped by AAudioServiceEndpointPlay::callbackLoop ("continue; // dead stream") → r frozen. Device A/B: drain OFF during underflow → up_fill 0→128, r froze @252ms, suspend logged; drain ON → up_fill stayed 5-7, NO suspend, r advanced. Self-recovers when writes resume (write drains → "Queue no longer full. Un-suspending").
NOTES=KEY INSIGHT: bug#1 (permanent silent call needing relaunch) ⟺ bug#3 (guest idle freeze). write_pcm_f32 drains the up-queue on EVERY call (even when it returns 0), so a call self-recovers as long as the guest keeps calling write. Permanent stall happens ONLY when the guest STOPS calling write_pcm_f32 for ~240ms+ during an underflow (= guest call loop falls into hrtimer_nanosleep idle). Fix space (OUT OF SCOPE this session): (a) host-side timer-driven up-queue drain independent of guest writes, or (b) host feeds silence on guest underrun (no underflow→no XRUN→no suspend), or (c) keep guest loop alive. Earpiece pin [2] -889s standalone (taimen quirk, separate=bug#5); reproduced on speaker [3] (USAGE_MEDIA legacy SHARED, same mixer path). Probe binary on device: /data/local/tmp/wart-host-probe97. Source: vendor/aosp-frameworks-av/services/oboeservice. Uncommitted: audio_impl.rs probe_call_stall + main.rs --probe-call-stall flag.
